  "congress": 116,
  "constitutionalAuthorityStatementText": "<pre>\n[Congressional Record Volume 165, Number 165 (Friday, October 18, 2019)]\n[House]\nFrom the Congressional Record Online through the Government Publishing Office [<a href=\"http://www.gpo.gov\">www.gpo.gov</a>]\nBy Mr. WALBERG:\nH.R. 4738.\nCongress has the power to enact this legislation pursuant\nto the following:\nArticle I, Section 8, Clause 3 of the Constitution of the\nUnited States; the power to regulate commerce among the\nseveral states.\nThe purpose of the bill is to amend the Civil Rights Act of\n1964 to provide protections against pregnancy discrimination\nin the workplace, and for other purposes.\n[Page H8259]\n</pre>",
